data.content:
Yes — MSTest v3.4+ supports **typed `DynamicData`** via tuples, eliminating the `object[]` casts:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[DynamicData(nameof(TestData))]
public void Validate_ReturnsExpected(string input, bool expected)
{
    var result = Validator.IsValid(input);
    Assert.AreEqual(expected, result);
}

public static IEnumerable<(string Input, bool Expected)> TestData =>
[
    ("valid@email.com", true),
    ("invalid", false),
    ("", false),
];
```

**Key differences:**
- Return `IEnumerable<(string, bool)>` instead of `IEnumerable<object[]>`
- Use tuple syntax `(...)` instead of array syntax `[...]`
- You get compile-time type checking — mismatched types won't compile

This requires **MSTest 3.4+** (the `Microsoft.Testing.Framework` / MSTest SDK). The test method signature stays the same; MSTest automatically destructures the tuple into the method parameters.
